QA5 M4. A named result that a deferred closure writes is a variable in memory,
and "return fmt.Errorf("f: %w", err)" is a store to it that reads it. The
load that the fmt.Errorf wraps runs before that store and before the deferred
call, so it reads neither: the Wrap is applied once, over what get returned.
The Error Set is the two forms run time has: ErrGet under the Wrap, and
ErrClose bare. (Before, each Sentinel was listed bare and under one to eight
nestings of the Wrap.)
-- args --
a.go:@t
-- stdout --
